# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Private financial data. NEVER commit any of this: the ledger, its backups,
# institution exports, and download logs all contain real account activity.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
data/
*.db
*.db-journal
*.db-wal
*.db-shm
*.bak
*.QIF
*.qif
*.ofx
*.qfx
*.OFX
*.QFX
!mammon/tests/fixtures/*
download.log
*_crash.log

# Internal planning docs — never check in, and keep their names out of every
# tracked file (so a grep of the committed tree never mentions them): match the
# private roadmap and design-plan docs by SHAPE, not by literal name. The
# *_roadmap.md and *_plan.md globs match only those two private docs under docs/;
# the tracked docs/qif_import_research.md is a *_research.md and is deliberately
# NOT covered by a wildcard, so it is listed nowhere here.
docs/*_roadmap.md
docs/quicken_research.md
docs/priorities_proposal_2026-09.md
docs/upgrade_priorities.md
docs/*_plan.md
# Design docs are internal planning notes, matched by SHAPE like the globs above.
# (amazon_itemization_design.md and investment_central_design.md predate this rule
# and stay tracked by explicit add -- git honours an explicit add over an ignore, so
# this glob does not untrack them; it keeps NEW design docs, e.g. the crypto redesign,
# private by default.)
docs/*_design.md
# Research/taxonomy working docs are the same kind of artifact: an undecided
# proposal that quotes the user verbatim, whose public form is an SRD section.
# Matched by SHAPE for the same reason as the globs above.
docs/*_taxonomy.md

# Build output: PyInstaller's dist/build, and the icon preview blowups.
build/
dist/
*.spec.bak

# Editor / vault state, personal to one machine.
.obsidian/

# Credentials / local config
.env
*.key
.claude/settings.local.json

# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.venv/
venv/

# Tooling
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.idea/
.vscode/
